---
import TVLayout from '../layouts/TVLayout.astro'
---

<TVLayout>
  <article class="bio">
    <h1 class="sr-only">Likith Shetty — AI/ML Engineer in Bengaluru</h1>
    <p class="big-text">
      Hi! I'm <span class="bio__photo" tabindex="0">Likith Shetty</span>, based in
      <span class="keep-together"
        ><button class="button-text js-channel-trigger" data-channel="9"
          >Bengaluru</button
        >.</span
      > I'm currently pursuing an M.Sc. in AI and Machine Learning at
      <a
        href="https://christuniversity.in"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">CHRIST University</a
      >, and I build agents, retrieval systems and the occasional optimizer.
      <br /><br />Most of what I make ends up on
      <a
        href="https://github.com/LikithSh3tty"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
      >: a support desk that answers out of product
      docs by meaning rather than keywords, a drift watchman that investigates a
      model before it retrains it, an income tracker that does an agency's
      accounting, and a packer that fits the most whole cells into an awkward
      shape. Two of them are <a href="/websites/">live</a>.
      <br /><br />I like systems that admit when they don't know something. Every
      one of those four will tell you it isn't sure rather than guess at an
      answer. The support desk runs its whole search on a model small enough to
      live inside the function, which costs nothing per query and never phones
      anyone. I wrote about
      <a
        href="https://medium.com/@shettylikith.rajesh/why-small-language-models-might-be-the-future-c714fcea4548"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">why small models might be the future</a
      > if that sounds like an odd choice.
      <br /><br />Before this I interned at
      <a
        href="https://www.paynearby.in/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">PayNearby</a
      > in Mumbai and led the IT Club at Nitte University. There's a
      <a href="/resume" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">resume</a> if you
      want the long version.
      <br /><br />Almost none of it gets written in silence. Here are the
      <a href="/playlists">playlists</a> if you want them.
      <br /><br />If you'd like to chat, reach me by
      <a href="mailto:likithshetty188@gmail.com">e-mail</a> or on
      <a
        href="https://linkedin.com/in/likith-shetty"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</TVLayout>

<style>
  /* A <button> is an atomic inline, so the browser may break between it and
     the punctuation that follows, orphaning the full stop on the next line. */
  .keep-together {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .bio__photo {
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);

    &::after {
      content: '';
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      z-index: var(--layer-me-hover);
      top: calc(100% + 1em);
      left: 1rem;
      width: 14rem;
      padding-bottom: 14rem;
      visibility: hidden;
      background-size: cover;
    }

    &:hover::after,
    &:focus::after {
      background-image: url(/assets/images/me.png);
      transition: visibility 0s 0.2s;
      visibility: visible;
    }
  }
</style>
